<title>UK: Sainsbury Reward gives 2-3 pct sales lift.</title>
<headline>Sainsbury Reward gives 2-3 pct sales lift.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British supermarket chain J. Sainsbury Plc is seeing a 2-3 percent uplift in sales following the launch of its Reward loyalty card in June, deputy chief executive Dino Adriano told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;We said when we launched it that we needed an uplift of something like 2-3 percent to cover its costs and that's what it's doing,&quot; Adriano said.</p>
</text>
